Emily Johnson.

183
00:10:34,750 --> 00:10:34,990
Emily.

184
00:10:35,330 --> 00:10:35,850
Yes, that's me.

185
00:10:36,150 --> 00:10:36,510
Hi, Emily.

186
00:10:36,650 --> 00:10:37,090
Mr. Carter.

187
00:10:37,450 --> 00:10:38,850
I'm Mr. Carter, the HR manager.

188
00:10:38,990 --> 00:10:39,550
Nice to meet you.

189
00:10:39,690 --> 00:10:40,530
Thanks for coming in today.

190
00:10:40,670 --> 00:10:40,890
Emily.

191
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:42,180
Nice to meet you too, Mr. Carter.

192
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:42,840
Thank you for having me.

193
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:43,380
Mr. Carter.

194
00:10:43,540 --> 00:10:43,880
Of course.

195
00:10:44,460 --> 00:10:45,100
Please have a seat.

196
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:46,320
How was your trip over here?

197
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,600
Did you find the office okay?

198
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:48,140
Emily.

199
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,200
Yes, it was pretty easy.

200
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:52,150
The directions were clear and traffic wasn't too bad this morning.

201
00:10:52,490 --> 00:10:53,010
Mr. Carter.

202
00:10:53,530 --> 00:10:54,130
Glad to hear that.

203
00:10:54,490 --> 00:10:57,130
We try to make things as smooth as possible for our candidates.

204
00:10:57,110 --> 00:10:59,030
Would you like some water or coffee before we begin?

205
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:00,410
Emily?

206
00:11:00,430 --> 00:11:00,940
No, I'm fine.

207
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:02,040
Thank you, Mr. Carter.

208
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:02,500
All right, then.

209
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:05,020
So let's get started.

210
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:05,580
Okay.

211
00:11:06,300 --> 00:11:08,470
Okay, let's just quickly break down those first few moments.

212
00:11:08,850 --> 00:11:10,150
It seems like basic politeness, right?

213
00:11:10,330 --> 00:11:11,370
Small talk.

214
00:11:11,390 --> 00:11:13,120
But Emily's approach here, it says a lot.

215
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:19,850
How does this initial back and forth, her sort of calm way of responding, her professional politeness, set a good tone right away?

216
00:11:20,270 --> 00:11:23,470
What's really being communicated even before the real questions start?

217
00:11:23,570 --> 00:11:32,180
You know, this is actually a mini masterclass in nonverbal communication and building rapport, even before they get into the substance.

218
00:11:32,810 --> 00:11:34,610
Emily's responses, they're composed.

219
00:11:34,630 --> 00:11:35,190
That greeting.

220
00:11:35,650 --> 00:11:36,750
Nice to meet you too, Mr. Carter.

221
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:37,620
Thank you for having me.

222
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,820
It's confident, but also respectful, humble even.

223
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:42,840
It hits the right note.

224
00:11:43,090 --> 00:11:46,260
And her answer about the trip, yes, it was pretty easy.

225
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:48,780
The directions were clear and traffic wasn't too bad.

226
00:11:49,140 --> 00:11:49,700
It's brief.

227
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:50,660
It's positive.

228
00:11:51,130 --> 00:11:59,760
It shows she's, well, observant, polite, and she can handle that kind of informal chat gracefully, which is a key part of business English, right?

229
00:11:59,820 --> 00:12:01,020
Not just the formal stuff.

230
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:02,500
She didn't complain about traffic or anything.

231
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,060
Exactly.

232
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:04,950
No oversharing, no negativity.

233
00:12:04,990 --> 00:12:08,570
These little interactions, they seem small, but they're incredibly important.

234
00:12:08,890 --> 00:12:11,160
It taps into that whole science of first impressions.

235
00:12:11,220 --> 00:12:13,960
People make judgments really fast within seconds sometimes.

236
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:14,420
Yeah.

237
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:19,650
So Emily here demonstrates social intelligence, a calm presence, even though she's probably nervous.

238
00:12:19,890 --> 00:12:22,130
And she shows appreciation for the interviewer's time.

239
00:12:22,430 --> 00:12:24,630
It signals she's thoughtful, appreciative, composed.

240
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:30,900
It builds rapport right from the start, making Mr. Carter more likely to listen positively to what she says later.

241
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:33,770
